0..78 Comment "// A flow between types written as the relation `A ⇝ B`, also `A ~~> B`: the"
79..157 Comment "// type-level spelling of `Flow(Type, A, B)`, introduced by `Flow.into` over a"
158..233 Comment "// translator. Under directed univalence a flow between types is a function"
234..307 Comment "// (Gratzer, Weinberger and Buchholtz, _Directed univalence in simplicial"
308..377 Comment "// homotopy type theory_, arXiv:2407.09146, Definition 1.2), so `⇝`"
378..455 Comment "// abbreviates the flow itself and no record of round trips stands beside it."
457..519 Comment "// The old and the new schema and the translator between them."
